@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] marshall-durable-authority
Marshall instances MUST use shared PostgreSQL as durable authority for VM intent,
reservations, access and terminal leases. Local processes, caches and PubSub
notifications MUST NOT independently authorize mutations after database authority
has expired or changed.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] marshall-independent-release
The production Marshall release MUST NOT depend on Lilly's or Porsche's application runtime.
Test-only dependencies MAY exercise real client/server boundaries; shared
production wire types and validation belong in protocol/.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] marshall-gate-preservation
Marshall precommit MUST retain the pinned-runtime, ADR, contract, compiler,
formatting, distributed-test, browser-state and forced Dialyzer checks. Any
upstream typespec exclusion MUST NOT suppress application findings, and unused
exclusions MUST be reported.
